Expected elements: present

Identity bar with the real hash, `block 63675` and an exit to `aztec-testnet`; stepping groups, `128 / 345`, phase rail; no band above the bar; the provenance marker is the Transaction pane's first row — `DATA`, a green-toned `Real Aztec testnet data` badge, the capture's own sentences. Code, Call Trace and Values each explain the missing symbols; `Supply sources` is present; no fixture content, no invented source, no engine-failure banner.

The badge's tone is affirmative and does not contradict its label, so it is not a presence failure — but it is the same green pill as `Succeeded` and `Trace ready`, so one hue now carries three unrelated meanings (execution outcome, replay readiness, data provenance) within 500px, and the provenance claim is coloured as a status. Beneath that, this light theme reads as inherited rather than designed for the register: canvas, pane body and pane header sit within a few percent of white and are separated only by hairlines, so across two mostly empty panes the structure nearly disappears and the emptiness has no tone distinguishing "nothing to show" from "not yet painted" — with `Engine loading` visible in the bar, that ambiguity is live. Three different blues do loading and navigation work in one bar, and the raw JSON block is the only tinted surface yet carries no token colour at all.

Highest-priority fixes: give provenance its own tone, distinct from status green; separate canvas from pane surface.

Rating: 6/10

